% =====================================================================
% art4_thresholds.clausal -- Art 4 threshold values for EU public procurement.
% Stores raw period facts and exposes query predicates.
% Source: EU Directive 2014/24/EU Art 4 + biennial delegated regulations.
% All monetary amounts in plain integer euro-cents.
% Library module: no verdict, no oracle, no manifest.yaml.
% =====================================================================

:- module(art4_thresholds, [
    art4_threshold/4,
    current_art4_threshold/3
]).

:- use_module(library(clpz)).

% (Clausal Prolog: date/3 from date_time is a plain term built and taken apart
% by unification, so it needs no import. The seam import of the seven
% contracting-authority and contract-type ATOMS from
% eu.procurement.directive_2014_24.vocabulary has no counterpart either: atoms
% need no import, and this file uses none of that module's predicates. euro and
% eur_cent from european_union were units; see the table below.)
:- use_module(kit/deadline_lib, [date_before/2, date_after/2, date_on_or_before/2, date_on_or_after/2]).

% The Art 4 threshold table, ONE declaration. Amounts declared in BASE
% currency (_tools/MIGRATION-money-constants.md) so the value and its
% currency are facts the engine holds; art4_threshold_value/5 keeps its
% name, arity and cents value type, DERIVED, so art4_threshold/4 and
% every one of the fourteen consumer domains is untouched.
%
% Clausal Prolog: the seam declared the table with
% -constants_number_currency(art4_threshold_amount/5, [...], euro, money_at(5)):
% 72 rows whose fifth argument is a value united in euro. Clausal Prolog has no
% united values and an ISO term cannot carry a unit, so each row is a FACT of
% the same name and arity, art4_threshold_amount/5, whose fifth argument is the
% statute's euro figure as a plain integer (the unit is euro, for every row).
% The seam's digit separators (5_225_000) are written without them (5225000).
art4_threshold_amount(works, central_government_authority,
    date(2016, 1, 1), date(2018, 1, 1), 5225000).
art4_threshold_amount(works, sub_central_contracting_authority,
    date(2016, 1, 1), date(2018, 1, 1), 5225000).
art4_threshold_amount(works, body_governed_by_public_law,
    date(2016, 1, 1), date(2018, 1, 1), 5225000).
art4_threshold_amount(supplies, central_government_authority,
    date(2016, 1, 1), date(2018, 1, 1), 135000).
